Subject: JSON.parse reads an expected plain key and its string or number value in place

What this does
  In the direct parser's object loop, when the shape chain is matched and its next key is plain, the input is compared with the key's bytes in place; when they match and the value starts a string or a number, the value is read there (json_parse_string / json_parse_number) and stored with the cached next shape (json_obj_adopt_shape). No key token, no atom reference taken and dropped, no recursive json_fast_value call for the value. Anything else (other key, other value type, a malformed value) continues on the existing path from the same byte.

Why we need it
  Most members of app records are expected keys with string or number values; the key token, the atom count traffic and the per-value call were a fifth of parse cycles. json_app parse only: -9.3% cycles, -6.1% instructions.

Soundness
  A plain cached key is an 8-bit string of bytes the key scanner accepts unchanged, so equal bytes followed by a quote are that key, and atoms are unique per string, so this is the transition json_obj_add would take (same checks: matched chain, current shape is the chain's k-th, the next shape differs). The atom is borrowed from the chain: between the comparison and the store only the string or number reader runs, which touches no shape cache. The value readers and their checks (leading zero, lone minus) are the ones json_fast_value uses, and a failure returns to the general parser, which re-parses the input and raises its own error. Differentials identical old vs new, including error names and messages: new jrec.js (6,120 inputs: every byte of a warm record deleted, truncated there, replaced by 15 bytes or given whitespace, parsed after two matching records and alone), jslot, jdiff, jdiff2, jedge, jscan, jnum, jld.

diff --git a/quickjs.c b/quickjs.c
index 4eb9230..d31a077 100644
--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -106689,6 +106689,49 @@ static int json_fast_value(JSParseState *s, const uint8_t **pp, int depth, JSVal
                     if (*p != '"')
                         goto obj_fail;
                     p++;
+                    /* the expected next key, plain, with a primitive value: its bytes compared in place, the value read here and
+                       stored with the cached shape; the key atom is only borrowed from the chain, which nothing changes before the
+                       store (a string or number reader touches no shape cache) */
+                    if (jsc && matched && k < jsc->n && jsc->plain[k] && jsc->shapes[k] == jsobj->shape &&
+                        jsc->shapes[k + 1] != jsc->shapes[k]) {
+                        JSString *ap = ctx->rt->atom_array[jsc->atoms[k]];
+                        uint32_t n = ap->len;
+                        const uint8_t *q;
+                        if ((size_t)(s->buf_end - p) > n + 1 && p[n] == '"' && memcmp(json_str8(ap), p, n) == 0) {
+                            q = json_fast_ws(p + n + 1);
+                            if (*q == ':') {
+                                q = json_fast_ws(q + 1);
+                                if (*q == '"' || *q == '-' || is_digit(*q)) {
+                                    if (*q == '"') {
+                                        q++;
+                                        if (json_parse_string(s, &q))
+                                            goto obj_fail;
+                                        prop_val = s->token.u.str.str;
+                                    } else {
+                                        const uint8_t *d = q + (*q == '-');
+                                        if (!is_digit(*d) || (d[0] == '0' && is_digit(d[1])))
+                                            goto obj_fail;
+                                        if (json_parse_number(s, &q))
+                                            goto obj_fail;
+                                        prop_val = s->token.u.num.val;
+                                    }
+                                    s->token.val = ' ';
+                                    if (json_obj_adopt_shape(ctx, jsobj, jsc->shapes[k + 1], prop_val)) {
+                                        JS_FreeValue(ctx, prop_val);
